 "captions": [
  {
   "text": "Imagine surviving an atomic bomb.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 2.86
  },
  {
   "text": "Now imagine getting on a train,",
   "start": 3.16,
   "end": 5.48
  },
  {
   "text": "traveling to another city,",
   "start": 5.48,
   "end": 7.24
  },
  {
   "text": "and getting hit by a second one.",
   "start": 7.24,
   "end": 9.52
  },
  {
   "text": "Three days later,",
   "start": 9.74,
   "end": 11.26
  },
  {
   "text": "this actually happened.",
   "start": 11.26,
   "end": 12.78
  },
  {
   "text": "His name was Tsutomu Yamaguchi.",
   "start": 12.8,
   "end": 15.48
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1945 Tsutomu was a 29-year-old",
   "start": 15.48,
   "end": 18.62
  },
  {
   "text": "engineer who designed oil tankers",
   "start": 18.62,
   "end": 20.66
  },
  {
   "text": "for Mitsubishi in his hometown",
   "start": 20.66,
   "end": 22.18
  },
  {
   "text": "of Nagasaki.",
   "start": 22.18,
   "end": 23.68
  },
  {
   "text": "That summer,",
   "start": 24.08,
   "end": 25.12
  },
  {
   "text": "his company sent him on a three-month",
   "start": 25.12,
   "end": 27.08
  },
  {
   "text": "business trip to Hiroshima.",
   "start": 27.08,
   "end": 29.32
  },
  {
   "text": "On August 6th,",
   "start": 29.44,
   "end": 31.46
  },
  {
   "text": "it was his last day there.",
   "start": 31.46,
   "end": 33.62
  },
  {
   "text": "Tomorrow,",
   "start": 33.98,
   "end": 34.62
  },
  {
   "text": "he'd finally go home to",
   "start": 34.62,
   "end": 36.08
  },
  {
   "text": "his wife and baby son.",
   "start": 36.08,
   "end": 38.14
  },
  {
   "text": "That morning,",
   "start": 38.18,
   "end": 39.06
  },
  {
   "text": "he was walking to the shipyard when",
   "start": 39.06,
   "end": 40.68
  },
  {
   "text": "he heard a plane overhead.",
   "start": 40.68,
   "end": 43.1
  },
  {
   "text": "He looked up and saw something",
   "start": 43.44,
   "end": 45.18
  },
  {
   "text": "drifting down on a parachute.",
   "start": 45.18,
   "end": 47.4
  },
  {
   "text": "Then,",
   "start": 47.94,
   "end": 48.8
  },
  {
   "text": "a flash brighter than the sun.",
   "start": 48.8,
   "end": 51.68
  },
  {
   "text": "He was about three kilometers",
   "start": 51.68,
   "end": 53.14
  },
  {
   "text": "from the blast.",
   "start": 53.14,
   "end": 54.66
  },
  {
   "text": "The shock wave threw",
   "start": 54.66,
   "end": 56.54
  },
  {
   "text": "him to the ground.",
   "start": 56.54,
   "end": 58.6
  },
  {
   "text": "His eardrums burst.",
   "start": 59.06,
   "end": 60.68
  },
  {
   "text": "The left side of his upper",
   "start": 61.2,
   "end": 62.68
  },
  {
   "text": "body was badly burned.",
   "start": 62.68,
   "end": 64.98
  },
  {
   "text": "When he looked up,",
   "start": 65.46,
   "end": 66.6
  },
  {
   "text": "a giant mushroom cloud was",
   "start": 66.6,
   "end": 68.1
  },
  {
   "text": "rising over the city.",
   "start": 68.1,
   "end": 69.66
  },
  {
   "text": "He spent the night in",
   "start": 69.66,
   "end": 70.68
  },
  {
   "text": "an air raid shelter.",
   "start": 70.68,
   "end": 72.18
  },
  {
   "text": "The next morning,",
   "start": 72.26,
   "end": 73.34
  },
  {
   "text": "he made his way to the station,",
   "start": 73.34,
   "end": 75.3
  },
  {
   "text": "found one of the few trains",
   "start": 75.3,
   "end": 76.54
  },
  {
   "text": "still running,",
   "start": 76.54,
   "end": 77.54
  },
  {
   "text": "and rode it home to Nagasaki.",
   "start": 77.54,
   "end": 79.74
  },
  {
   "text": "Wrapped in bandages,",
   "start": 79.94,
   "end": 81.64
  },
  {
   "text": "exhausted,",
   "start": 81.64,
   "end": 82.66
  },
  {
   "text": "he had survived the unthinkable.",
   "start": 82.8,
   "end": 84.9
  },
  {
   "text": "Surely,",
   "start": 85.02,
   "end": 85.64
  },
  {
   "text": "the worst was over.",
   "start": 85.64,
   "end": 87.16
  },
  {
   "text": "On August 9th,",
   "start": 87.38,
   "end": 89.1
  },
  {
   "text": "he insisted on going back to work.",
   "start": 89.1,
   "end": 91.54
  },
  {
   "text": "He was telling his supervisor",
   "start": 91.68,
   "end": 92.96
  },
  {
   "text": "what he'd seen.",
   "start": 92.96,
   "end": 95.0
  },
  {
   "text": "One bomb destroying",
   "start": 95.24,
   "end": 96.36
  },
  {
   "text": "an entire city.",
   "start": 96.36,
   "end": 98.08
  },
  {
   "text": "His boss didn't believe him.",
   "start": 98.52,
   "end": 100.58
  },
  {
   "text": "That's impossible,",
   "start": 100.76,
   "end": 102.08
  },
  {
   "text": "he said.",
   "start": 102.08,
   "end": 103.12
  },
  {
   "text": "One bomb can't do that.",
   "start": 103.28,
   "end": 105.58
  },
  {
   "text": "And at that exact moment,",
   "start": 105.78,
   "end": 107.96
  },
  {
   "text": "the room filled with the same",
   "start": 107.96,
   "end": 109.62
  },
  {
   "text": "blinding white light.",
   "start": 109.62,
   "end": 111.9
  },
  {
   "text": "Once again,",
   "start": 112.44,
   "end": 113.66
  },
  {
   "text": "Tsutomu was about three kilometers",
   "start": 113.84,
   "end": 116.02
  },
  {
   "text": "from ground zero.",
   "start": 116.02,
   "end": 118.12
  },
  {
   "text": "Somehow,",
   "start": 118.12,
   "end": 118.72
  },
  {
   "text": "he survived again.",
   "start": 118.72,
   "end": 120.74
  },
  {
   "text": "His bandages were torn off,",
   "start": 121.06,
   "end": 123.02
  },
  {
   "text": "and he fell sick with fever",
   "start": 123.02,
   "end": 124.34
  },
  {
   "text": "for over a week.",
   "start": 124.34,
   "end": 125.92
  },
  {
   "text": "But his wife and son",
   "start": 126.98,
   "end": 128.38
  },
  {
   "text": "had also survived.",
   "start": 128.38,
   "end": 130.38
  },
  {
   "text": "And Tsutomu went on to",
   "start": 130.56,
   "end": 133.12
  },
  {
   "text": "live a long life.",
   "start": 133.12,
   "end": 134.88
  },
  {
   "text": "He had more children,",
   "start": 135.14,
   "end": 136.58
  },
  {
   "text": "worked as a teacher,",
   "start": 136.58,
   "end": 137.76
  },
  {
   "text": "and an engineer again.",
   "start": 137.76,
   "end": 139.86
  },
  {
   "text": "And in 2009,",
   "start": 140.26,
   "end": 141.78
  },
  {
   "text": "the Japanese government officially",
   "start": 141.78,
   "end": 143.36
  },
  {
   "text": "recognized him as a survivor",
   "start": 143.36,
   "end": 145.2
  },
  {
   "text": "of both bombings,",
   "start": 145.2,
   "end": 147.0
  },
  {
   "text": "the only person ever formally",
   "start": 147.04,
   "end": 148.84
  },
  {
   "text": "given that status.",
   "start": 148.84,
   "end": 150.86
  },
  {
   "text": "In his later years,",
   "start": 150.86,
   "end": 152.04
  },
  {
   "text": "he traveled and spoke out",
   "start": 152.04,
   "end": 153.22
  },
  {
   "text": "against nuclear weapons,",
   "start": 153.22,
   "end": 154.82
  },
  {
   "text": "so no one would ever experience",
   "start": 154.82,
   "end": 156.36
  },
  {
   "text": "what he did.",
   "start": 156.36,
   "end": 157.72
  },
  {
   "text": "Twice.",
   "start": 158.0,
   "end": 158.84
  },
  {
   "text": "Tsutomu Yamaguchi died in",
   "start": 159.4,
   "end": 161.1
  },
  {
   "text": "2010 at the age of 93.",
   "start": 161.1,
   "end": 163.78
  },
  {
   "text": "Some people call him the unluckiest",
   "start": 164.4,
   "end": 165.96
  },
  {
   "text": "man in history.",
   "start": 165.96,
   "end": 167.36
  },
  {
   "text": "Others call him the luckiest.",
   "start": 167.7,
   "end": 169.6
  },
  {
   "text": "What do you think?",
   "start": 169.82,
   "end": 171.22
  },
  {
   "text": "Tell me in the comments and subscribe",
   "start": 171.32,
   "end": 172.9
  },
  {
   "text": "for more stories that sound too",
   "start": 172.9,
   "end": 174.62
  },
  {
   "text": "crazy to be true.",
   "start": 174.62,
   "end": 176.1
  }
 ],
